// EXPECT: E0218 — a view has no `.data` (ADR-0044 §4)
// Deliberately absent, for the reason `[N]T`'s is (ADR-0039 §5). `string.data` exists only because ADR-0004
// fixed that layout for the FFI boundary, which a view does not cross.
//
// **The original reason has expired, and the refusal still stands — for a better one.** ADR-0044 §4 argued that
// `.data` "would hand out an unbounded `*T` one wave after the bounds check was added, and there is no pointer
// arithmetic to use it with". Both halves are now false: pointer arithmetic arrived in ADR-0064, and typed
// allocation (ADR-0106) makes a `*T` an ordinary thing to hold. ADR-0109 revisited the refusal rather than
// inheriting it — the third time this project has found a stated reason outliving its truth.
//
// What it found is that a caller reaching for `.data` wants to build a **view**, and the answer is the missing
// *constructor* rather than the exposed field: `view(p, n)` builds a `[]T` from a pointer and a count, which is
// what `List.elements` hands to `Sort`. So `.data` stays absent because nothing needs it, which is a better
// reason than the one it replaced.
first :: (xs: []u8) -> *u8 {
    return xs.data;
}

main :: () {
    buf: [3]u8;
    p := first(buf[]);
}
